{title: O Hanukkah}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Am]Hanukkah, Oh Hanukkah
Come light the menorah
[Am]Let’s have a party
We’[G]ll all dance the [C]hora
[Am]Gather round the [G]table,
We’ll [C]give you a [C/B]treat.
[Am]Dreidels to play with [E7]and [Am]latkes to eat
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
And [Am]while we are [Am]playing,
The [C]candles are [G]burning [C]low. [E7]
[Am]One for each [Dm]night, they [Am]shed a sweet [Dm]light
To [Am]remind us of [E7]days long a[Am]go.
[Am]One for [Dm]each night, they [Am]shed a sweet [Dm]light
To re[Am]mind us of [E7]days long a[Am]go.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
*[Am]O Hanukkah! Hanukkah*
*[Am]O Hanukkah! Hanukkah*
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Fine}

{comment: Interlude}
[Am] [Dm] [Am] [Dm] [Am] [E7] [Am] [x2]

{comment: D.C. al Fine}
